// ch11 (round 2, R2-2 / #2227): a `require ... = #pkg:sha1:` pin at the
// top of an entry .vibe. Round 2 measured the lanes DISAGREEING about
// this file -- the FS build lane compiled it while `vibe check` answered
// `unexpected token: =` at the pin line. #2227's fix blanks the pin head
// in check's pre-parse exactly as every build-lane ingestion does, so
// now every lane agrees: the probe compiles, prints below, and the
// check directive answers clean (empty output, exit 0). The unused pin
// verifies nothing -- pin verification still fires when the package is
// actually imported (gate 6c).
//! cli: check
require @vibe/core 0.2.0 = #pkg:sha1:0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

fn main with Console {
  println("pin head parsed")
}
